    {
      "text": "We need the number of trailing zeros in \\(1000!\\).  \nTrailing zeros come from factors of 10, i.e., pairs of 2 and 5. Since there are more factors of 2 than 5, we count factors of 5.\n\n\\[\n\\left\\lfloor \\frac{1000}{5} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{1000}{25} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{1000}{125} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{1000}{625} \\right\\rfloor\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 200 + 40 + 8 + 1 = 249\n\\]\n\nThe answer is 249.",
      "usage": {
